/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  F23b -- Hagen-Poiseuille wedge.  THE ONE SUBSTANTIVE DICTIONARY CHANGE from
  F23 (pre-registration section 5.3), and the reason F23b exists at all.

  F23's coarse and medium levels were NEVER ITERATIVELY CONVERGED: their Ux
  initial residuals sat 7,300x and 26,000x the registered floor at iteration
  4000 and the flow was STILL ACCELERATING FROM REST.  Section 5.2 measured the
  mechanism: the OUTER SIMPLE loop is the bottleneck, not the linear solver.
  GAMG reported `No Iterations 1` for Ux at every iteration -- the inner solve
  reaches its relTol in one V-cycle and is doing its job -- while the relaxed
  Picard iteration crawled at 1 - O((h/R)^2), measured 8.190e-04 (NR = 64) and
  2.065e-04 (NR = 128), a ratio of 3.96 ~ h^-2.  Extrapolated: coarse ~25,000,
  medium ~100,000, fine ~395,000 iterations.  F23's ladder was not runnable at
  4,000 iterations and was not runnable at ANY cap the lab would grant.

  `consistent yes` is SIMPLEC, whose whole purpose is to allow alpha_U -> 1.  At
  alpha_U = 1 the added diagonal ((1-a)/a) diag(A_P) VANISHES and the outer loop
  converges at the inner solve's own rate, in a handful of iterations rather
  than 10^5.

  THIS IS A PREDICTION, NOT A MEASUREMENT, and it is registered as one: nothing
  had been launched when it was written.  Section 5.5's ARM-P tests it under the
  freeze sha, ARM-F (alpha_U = 0.9) is the registered fallback, and a double
  failure HALTs the rung as BLOCKED rather than taking a third setting -- a
  third setting chosen after watching two fail is a parameter hunt, and a
  parameter hunt is not a registration.

  NO residualControl: the run goes to endTime and the section 5.4 plateau gate
  decides.  pRefCell/pRefValue pin the pressure level of the cyclic domain.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object fvSolution; }

solvers
{
    p
    {
        solver          GAMG;
        smoother        GaussSeidel;
        tolerance       1e-12;
        relTol          1e-4;
    }
    U
    {
        solver          GAMG;
        smoother        GaussSeidel;
        tolerance       1e-14;
        relTol          1e-4;
    }
}

SIMPLE
{
    nNonOrthogonalCorrectors 0;
    consistent      yes;
    pRefCell        0;
    pRefValue       0;
    // NO residualControl: the run goes to endTime and the grader's Class C
    // plateau gate decides whether it plateaued.
}

relaxationFactors
{
    fields    { p 1.0; }
    equations { U 1.0; }
}
